  "runtimeAcceptance": [
    "Review at the owner's 40-degree camera on desktop and iPad, including portrait and landscape HUD occlusion.",
    "Each changed route and hunt court must remain connected; do not turn the open world into a corridor maze.",
    "Collision and visible cliff boundaries must share one authored footprint; cliffs are never decorative walk-through surfaces.",
    "Use a continuous heightfield with ramps for all traversable elevations; do not author traversable overhangs or a bridge-over-road without explicit engine support.",
    "Keep the default source look. PR137 cel/frieren are opt-in experiments, not an owner approval to change the game's palette.",
    "At pitch40, projected ground occlusion is roughly h / tan(40deg) = 1.19h before perspective. Use this as an initial placement estimate only; verify actual projected silhouettes, hero, enemies, telegraphs, loot and touch targets.",
    "Put the largest masses behind or beside combat. Foreground close to the player uses low objects or proven hero/enemy visibility treatment.",
    "New modules must share materials, batch by bounded spatial cells, reuse existing resident preparation/disposal, and avoid large transparent overdraw or per-frame scene assembly.",
    "Measure rendering counts and memory against matched 40-degree source cameras. No FPS or percent-quality claim without device evidence."
  ],
  "heightDefinition": "Terrain height ranges specify proposed relief above the local lower grade, not an additive raise on top of existing plateaus."
}
